<title>MEXICO: Mexico's Cydsa to pay 0.50 peso dividend.</title>
<headline>Mexico's Cydsa to pay 0.50 peso dividend.</headline>
<dateline>MONTERREY, Mexico</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shareholders for the Monterrey-based chemical company Celulosa y Derivados SA (Cydsa) have approved a dividend of 0.50 pesos per share, a company spokesman said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;A dividend payment of 50 centavos per share was approved, payable on May 6,&quot; Tomas Gonzalez Sada, a spokesman for Cydsa, told Reuters.</p>
<p>The company will pay out a total of 60 million pesos corresponding to 120 million shares, he said.</p>
<p>The dividend is valid for coupon 49, Gonzalez said.</p>
<p>((--Jacqueline Lerma, Monterrey bureau, +528 345-7677))</p>
